diagnostic_evidence.quote:
Solve the following subproblem 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:algorithmic:update}
    y^{n} = \argmin_u \left\{H^n(u) - \langle \nabla F^n(u^{n}),u\rangle + \frac12\|u-\hat{u}\|^2_M\right\}
\end{equation}

note that $y^n$ is a critical point of this convex function and $y^n$ satisfies the following optimality condition
    \begin{equation}\label{eq:subpro:optcon}
    \nabla H^n(y^n) -\nabla F^n(u^n)+ M(y^n - u^n) = 0.
    \end{equation}

If $h(u)=Au -b_0$, the equation \eqref{eq:solve:y:pre:general} can be reformulated as the following preconditioned iteration 
\begin{equation}
    y^n =  \hat{u}^n + \mathbb{M}^{-1}(b^n - T\hat{u}^n),
\end{equation}

E^n(y^n + \lambda_n d^n)  \leq   E^n(y^n) -\alpha\lambda_n\|d^n\|^2, \ \lambda_n=  
     \begin{cases}
              \lambda_n, \ \ \text{if there exists a positive $\lambda_n>0$} \\
             0, \ \ \ \ \text{otherwise}
     \end{cases}
